ession search filter can be specified with\n                        '/<expression>'. eg. '-low,=done,-children' would show\n                        any notes with a priority less than or equal to 'low'\n                        that are marked as done and would not show child notes.\n-v, --verbose           Display verbosely.\n--colour ARG            Override default colours of todo items. Multiple colours\n                        can be specified, separated by commas. eg.\n                        high=red,medium=white. Items are bolded by prefixing\n                        them with a '+'.\n--mono                  Disable all use of colour.\n--force-colour          Force use of colour.\n--help                  Display this help.\n--version               Display version of todo.\n--title [ARG]           Set the title of this directory's todo notes.\n--date-format ARG       Format the display of time values. The format is that\n                        used by strftime(3).\n--format ARG            Specify a display format to use. ARG is in the form\n                        <key>=<format-string>.\n--use-format ARG        Map one format string to another (eg. --use-format\n","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"00e4df06-65b3-41e3-be02-46237d336908"},{"content":"Your previous reasoning (interrupted): The user wants to mark item 1 as done. I'll use `devtodo -G -d 1` to mark it as done. Maybe with a comment too using `-c`? Let me just mark it done. The `-c` option manipulates finishing comment when marking as done — it might prompt for a comment. Let me just do `-d 1` simply.","role":"system"},{"content":"","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"command\":\"devtodo -G -d 1\"}","name":"bash"},"id":"594e6657-ba7f-4ef3-814b-8232e9a4b6bc","type":"function"}]},{"content":"(exit exit status: 0)","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"594e6657-ba7f-4ef3-814b-8232e9a4b6bc"},{"content":"Your previous reasoning (interrupted): The command succeeded. Let me verify by listing the