    "content": "Your previous reasoning (interrupted): Hmm, `all,/Test/` still returns nothing! But `+high` works and `-medium` works. Weird. So the search filter seems broken with -G? Or maybe the search expression is case-sensitive and... \"Test item beta\" definitely contains \"Test\".\n\nWait, maybe the search expression in the filter applies only to... hmm. Maybe there's a bug in devtodo where search only works on the directory database, not global? Or maybe the regex needs different quoting? When passed as `-f all,/Test/` — the shell passes it literally, fine.\n\nLet me try `-f /Test` without trailing slash, or lowercase `/test/`, or `/item/`. I tried `/item/` and `/beta/` before — nothing. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the search is done against the note body plus... hmm. Or maybe with -G the search database is different. Let me test search on a local database instead? Actually, let me try `--filter 'all,/.*/'` to see if search works at all with the global DB.\n\nActually wait — maybe the issue is that the global database flag changes what database the filter searches? Let me just test `devtodo -G -f 'all,/.*/'`. If that shows nothing, search is broken with -G. If it shows everything, then my regex was somehow wrong.",
