r of the symbol (point anywhere on the symbol's name).","type":"integer"},"include_declaration":{"description":"Whether to include the declaration site itself in the results. Default: true.","type":"boolean"},"line":{"description":"1-based line number of the symbol (point anywhere on the symbol's name).","type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"The .rs file containing the symbol (absolute path).","type":"string"}},"required":["path","line","column"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"List valid code completions (methods, fields, functions, variables) at a cursor position in a Rust file, via rust-analyzer. Use to discover what members a type has or what identifiers are in scope, without reading the source. Requires the LSP server to be running (lsp = on in config, or /lsp on).","name":"lsp_completion","parameters":{"properties":{"column":{"description":"1-based column number of the cursor position.","type":"integer"},"line":{"description":"1-based line number of the cursor position.","type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"The .rs file to complete in (absolute path).","type":"string"}},"required":["path","line","column"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}],"top_p":0.95}
