[2026-10-02 14:54:52 18daa3efd4a8d9a3] ASSISTANT: Here's the system prompt addition, based on everything I actually verified (including the quirks that cost me time today):

````markdown
## Managing the user's todo list (devtodo)

The user tracks todos with `devtodo`. **Always pass `-G`** (global database).
Without it, devtodo silently creates/uses a `.todo` file in the current directory.

### Commands
- Show open tasks:            `devtodo -G`
- Show all (done + subtasks): `devtodo -G -A`          (add `-v` for dates/priority/duration)
- Add task:                   `devtodo -G -a "Buy milk"`
- Add with priority:          `devtodo -G -a "Fix prod bug" -p veryhigh`
- Add subtask of item N:      `devtodo -G -a "step text" -g N`
- Mark done (incl. children): `devtodo -G -d N`         (`-D N` to un-done)
- Mark done + comment:        `devtodo -G -d N -c`      (prompts for a finishing comment)
- Remove item (incl. children): `devtodo -G --remove N`
- Move item A under B:        `devtodo -G -R A,B`       (`devtodo -G -R A` → back to root)
- Edit item N's text/priority: `devtodo -G -e N`        (see gotchas — prompts on stdin)

Priorities: `veryhigh`, `high`, `medium` (default), `low`, `verylow`.
After adding, devtodo prints `Index of new item is N` — use that index.

### Gotchas (verified on this system)
- **Indices are dynamic.** Items are sorted by priority, so adding a
  `veryhigh` item renumbers existing ones (and done items keep their indices,
  so they still count). List right before acting, and re-list after any add.
- **Removing a parent deletes its whole subtree.** To remove a subtask only,
  use its full index, e.g. `--remove 2.1`.
- **`-e` reads from stdin, not an editor app**: it prompts `text> ` then
  `priority [current] > `. Works non-interactively by piping:
  `printf 'new text\nhigh\n' | devtodo -G -e N`  (one line = keep priority).
  Empty stdin BLANKS the item text — never run `-e` without piping text.
- **`-a` without a note argument** also reads the note from stdin.
- Output markers: `-` prefix = done, no marker = open. Subtasks only appear
  with `-A`.
- Filters: `-f '=done'`, `-f '-done'`, `-f '+high'` (≥ high),
  `-f '-medium'` (≤ medium). The regex search filter (`-f /pattern/`) is
  **broken in the installed version** — search with
  `devtodo -G -A | grep -i pattern` instead.
````

The two most valuable lines are the dynamic-indices warning and the `-e`-reads-stdin trick — both are things I burned several minutes discovering today. Everything above was tested live, not copied from the man page (which is also why the broken search filter is flagged rather than recommended).

